💻 Cloud Shell Terminal

Cloud Shell Terminal is a browser-based command-line environment in Google Cloud. 
It allows developers to write and run Python/code, install packages, manage files, execute gcloud commands, and build/test AI applications directly inside Google Cloud.

=============

Think of it like this:

Cloud Shell Terminal = 💻 Your workshop
Agent Studio          = 🎨 Your AI design/testing workspace
=======


1. Cloud Shell Terminal

This is basically a Linux terminal inside Google Cloud.

---------------

You were doing things like:

pip install -U google-genai

and:

python test_gemini.py

---------

Your Python program then called:

Python
   ↓
Google Gen AI SDK
   ↓
Vertex AI
   ↓
Gemini

-----------

What Cloud Shell is good for

You can:

Write Python programs
Install Python packages
Run scripts
Create files
Use Git
Run gcloud commands
Build APIs
Build RAG applications
Build AI agents
Deploy applications

So Cloud Shell is a developer environment.

